{"ts": "2026-10-26T20:09:22.260232Z", "run_id": "r-20261026T2007Z-6906", "unit": "openspec:audit-queue-durable", "seq": 22, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-002", "id": "Q-002", "status": "answered", "reason": "The question asks a fact about external sinks that no repository document records, but the spec fixes the behaviour the blocked tasks must implement: 400, 413 and 422 are refusals, 2xx delivers, every other status is retried, and the scenario enumerates the retried statuses. design.md D3 gives the rationale and the \"Decisions taken without the owner\" section marks the set as reversible, so the implementation proceeds per spec and the external-sink uncertainty remains a note for the owner. The current queue.go confirms the retry limit being replaced, so no other code constrains the set.", "called": true, "tasks": ["1.1", "2.1", "3.1", "3.2"], "target": null, "kind": "ambiguous", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 0.85465425, "decision": "answer", "answer_sha256": "63bd3a61eefa5520bda7a009d7316294e1aed68d336dbb5287813dce34d6845c", "checked": [{"ref": "spec:specs/audit-queue/spec.md#requirement-an-event-the-sink-refuses-goes-to-the-dead-letter-file-on-its-first-answer", "quote": "A sink answer with status 400, 413 or 422 SHALL be a refusal: the sink read the request and will never accept it.", "claim": "The spec fixes the refusal set the implementation must use."}, {"ref": "spec:specs/audit-queue/spec.md#requirement-an-event-the-sink-refuses-goes-to-the-dead-letter-file-on-its-first-answer", "quote": "A 2xx answer SHALL deliver the event; every other status SHALL be retried.", "claim": "Every status outside 2xx and the refusal set is retried, leaving no room for a sink-specific set."}, {"ref": "spec:specs/audit-queue/spec.md#scenario-which-statuses-are-a-refusal", "quote": "for 401, 403, 404, 409, 429, 500, 502, 503 and 504 the sink receives at least 3 requests within 2 s, `DeadLetterTotal()` is 0", "claim": "The scenario enumerates the statuses that must be retried, so the set is tested and not open to widening."}, {"ref": "spec:design.md", "quote": "**D3. Which answers are final.** Only 400, 413 and 422 are a refusal: the sink parsed the request and will never", "claim": "The design decides the refusal set and gives the rationale for retrying 401, 403, 404, 408, 429 and 5xx."}, {"ref": "spec:design.md", "quote": "The refusal set (400, 413, 422) and retrying 403 (D3); defaults 4 and 1,000; the settings as environment", "claim": "The design records the refusal set as a decision taken without the owner that is reversible without a format change, so it does not block implementation."}, {"ref": "packages/go/auditq/queue.go:358", "quote": "func (q *Queue) emitWithRetry(e Event) {", "claim": "The current code dead-letters after a fixed retry count with no status-based refusal set, so no existing code constrains which statuses are final."}]}
